cff-version: 1.2.0
title: >-
  Cell-type-resolved drug target discovery in major depressive
  disorder: a reanalysis of GSE144136
message: If you use this code or its results, please cite it as below.
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Giuliana
    family-names: Vizino-Zambito
    affiliation: Department of Anatomy and Cell Biology, McGill University
abstract: >-
  An open, reproducible pipeline that reanalyses public single-nucleus RNA-seq
  data from the dorsolateral prefrontal cortex of men with major depressive
  disorder (GSE144136, Nagy et al. 2020), tests for cell-type-specific
  differential expression by pseudobulk, and ranks the resulting genes as
  candidate drug targets on evidence, druggability, brain specificity and
  cell-type specificity. The pipeline converges on the astrocyte receptor
  GPR37L1, and includes leave-one-donor-out, covariate and cross-cohort
  robustness checks.
keywords:
  - single-nucleus RNA-seq
  - major depressive disorder
  - astrocytes
  - drug target prioritisation
  - GPR37L1
license: MIT
date-released: '2026-11-16'
references:
